(6512095, 968249, 10785, '<td valign="top">You got a really good splash and shape to the crown. However, the focus totally missed the crown. I think a little tighter aperture would have helped you bring the whole scene into focus. I would have liked to see a whiter surrounding to make the purple stand out more. The creamy or grey color is not very complimentary to the purple.</td>', 'You got a really good splash and shape to the crown. However, the focus totally missed the crown. I think a little tighter aperture would have helped you bring the whole scene into focus. I would have liked to see a whiter surrounding to make the purple stand out more. The creamy or grey color is not very complimentary to the purple.', '2011-08-22 12:49:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512098, 968641, 59029, '<td valign="top">lovely eye colour.  Is it a Himmy, Birman or Raggie? :-)</td>', 'lovely eye colour.  Is it a Himmy, Birman or Raggie? :-)', '2011-08-22 12:51:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512102, 968643, 10785, '<td valign="top">Nice soft focus effect! A crop of the right side would give you nicely centered subjects for an 8x10 image suitable for any parents wall!! If you wanted to keep them offset in the frame, the subjects would be better shown on the right side of the frame leaving the left side empty given their angled composition. I think the only other thing to watch out for, which is probably not an issue for your full size image, is the stray hairs. Re-sizing has given the stray hairs the .jpg jaggies. But a beautiful child portrait for sure and very suitable for framing!</td>', 'Nice soft focus effect! A crop of the right side would give you nicely centered subjects for an 8x10 image suitable for any parents wall!! If you wanted to keep them offset in the frame, the subjects would be better shown on the right side of the frame leaving the left side empty given their angled composition. I think the only other thing to watch out for, which is probably not an issue for your full size image, is the stray hairs. Re-sizing has given the stray hairs the .jpg jaggies. But a beautiful child portrait for sure and very suitable for framing!', '2011-08-22 12:55:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512105, 967896, 59029, '<td valign="top">Good general idea but poorly thought out. There''s a reason why you very rarely see shots like this - half-eaten food being eaten just is not appealing.  Would have been far better to have had the model ABOUT to bite into a rack or ribs, not in the process of gnawing on one.</td>', 'Good general idea but poorly thought out. There''s a reason why you very rarely see shots like this - half-eaten food being eaten just is not appealing.  Would have been far better to have had the model ABOUT to bite into a rack or ribs, not in the process of gnawing on one.', '2011-08-22 12:56:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512106, 968041, 10785, '<td valign="top">Good colors and nice use of DoF to put the focal point right where it needs to be!! The background elements don''t take away from the subject and serve to add a much needed context! Apples and cinnamon are a yummy combination!</td>', 'Good colors and nice use of DoF to put the focal point right where it needs to be!! The background elements don''t take away from the subject and serve to add a much needed context! Apples and cinnamon are a yummy combination!', '2011-08-22 12:57:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512107, 968241, 59029, '<td valign="top">missed focus on the coffee itself knocks a point or two off of an otherwise decent shot.</td>', 'missed focus on the coffee itself knocks a point or two off of an otherwise decent shot.', '2011-08-22 12:57:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512111, 968526, 10785, '<td valign="top">Is there a support group for all the water drop and the glass people? Every challenge has these type of pictures. You can make them fit anything!! When in doubt, shoot a glass or a splash, or hey, combine them both!!!<br/> <br/>Now that my rant is over you have great lighting and color and splash and it fits the Challenge nicely! Lose the mirror''s edge if possible.</td>', 'Is there a support group for all the water drop and the glass people? Every challenge has these type of pictures. You can make them fit anything!! When in doubt, shoot a glass or a splash, or hey, combine them both!!! Now that my rant is over you have great lighting and color and splash and it fits the Challenge nicely! Lose the mirror''s edge if possible.', '2011-08-22 13:01:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512113, 968606, 99263, '<td valign="top">Great shot but what a terrible tragedy. Was this just before the actual moment it happened or was this on another occasion?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-08-29 02:28:22.</i></td>', 'Great shot but what a terrible tragedy. Was this just before the actual moment it happened or was this on another occasion?', '2011-08-22 13:02:06.000000', '2011-08-29 03:28:22.000000', 1),
(6512115, 967602, 10785, '<td valign="top">Very interesting viewpoint!</td>', 'Very interesting viewpoint!', '2011-08-22 13:04:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512120, 967905, 10785, '<td valign="top">It would have been much more effective if the focal point was actually on the clef symbol. However you did get great DoF, tones and I like the de-saturated look.</td>', 'It would have been much more effective if the focal point was actually on the clef symbol. However you did get great DoF, tones and I like the de-saturated look.', '2011-08-22 13:06:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6512124, 967925, 10785, '<td valign="top">It''s like a nightmare come true!</td>', 'It''s like a nightmare come true!', '2011-08-22 13:19:48.000000', NULL, 1),
